/-!
# The quadratic space of the Parker triality construction

This interface exports the 24-dimensional vector space with the twisted addition
of Aschbacher, *Sporadic Groups*, Exercise 4.6, p. 64. Its prescribed quadratic
form is nonsingular and has plus type, witnessed by the 12-dimensional subspace
of zero-code coordinates.

For the actual triality permutations, `q1Word_mul` gives an exact product law:
the word whose coordinates are the prescribed twisted sum differs from the
product by an explicit power of `z1N`. The resulting identities `q1Word_sq` and
`q1Word_commutator` give the source quadratic and polar values as binary
exponents of `z1N`; `q1Word_mul_mem_Q1CentralKernel` gives the product agreement
modulo the subgroup generated by `z1N` and `k1`.

The coordinate laws follow from Golay polarization and cocode duality, and the
word laws from the concrete action on loop triples. These calculations support
Section 27, pp. 144–145, independently of a global normal-form theorem. The
construction and kernel of the homomorphism on the whole subgroup `Q1` remain
separate quotient-theory obligations.
-/
